From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 05:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: a null CHARFORMAT is a format we do not know, not a
 crash.

Excel creating a new workbook takes the process down:

    wine: Unhandled page fault on read access to 0000000000000000
      at address 000000007B6F2326

which is riched20 +0x22326 -- and riched20 is one of ours, so addr2line puts
it exactly: cfany_to_cf2w, dlls/riched20/style.c:38, the function's first
statement, `from->cbSize`.

Both callers reach it with a pointer they did not create. handle_EM_SETCHARFORMAT
passes the message's lParam, which an application may set to anything.
ME_MakeEditor passes whatever ITextHost::TxGetCharFormat left in an out
parameter it only checked the HRESULT of -- and Excel implements ITextHost
itself, answering S_OK without filling that pointer. That is a thing a host
is allowed to do, and Windows' own riched20 evidently survives it.

The cbSize checks that follow already treat an unrecognised size as "not a
format I know" and return FALSE, so a null pointer belongs in the same bucket:
there is nothing to convert. The para.c caller additionally keeps the default
style it has already built rather than overwriting it from nothing.

Measured after: Excel reaches its Start screen, creates a blank workbook, and
renders the full grid, ribbon and status bar.
--- a/dlls/riched20/style.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/style.c
@@ -35,6 +35,23 @@
 
 BOOL cfany_to_cf2w(CHARFORMAT2W *to, const CHARFORMAT2W *from)
 {
+  /* Every caller reaches this with a pointer it did not create: one from an
+   * EM_SETCHARFORMAT lParam, one from whatever the host's ITextHost::
+   * TxGetCharFormat handed back. Neither is guaranteed non-NULL, and this
+   * function's first act is to dereference it.
+   *
+   * Measured: Excel creating a new workbook takes Wine down with
+   * "Unhandled page fault on read access to 0000000000000000" at
+   * riched20 +0x22326, which is exactly the `from->cbSize` below. Excel
+   * implements ITextHost itself; its TxGetCharFormat answers S_OK without
+   * filling the out pointer, which is a thing a host is allowed to do and
+   * which Windows' own riched20 evidently survives.
+   *
+   * The size checks that follow already treat an unrecognised cbSize as
+   * "not a format I know" and return FALSE, so a null pointer belongs in
+   * exactly the same bucket -- there is nothing to convert. */
+  if (!from) return FALSE;
+
   if (from->cbSize == sizeof(CHARFORMATA))
   {
     CHARFORMATA *f = (CHARFORMATA *)from;
--- a/dlls/riched20/para.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/para.c
@@ -192,12 +192,15 @@
   style = ME_MakeStyle(&cf);
   text->pDefaultStyle = style;
 
-  if (ITextHost_TxGetCharFormat(editor->texthost, &host_cf) == S_OK)
+  /* S_OK here does not promise a format: a host may report success and leave
+   * the out pointer alone (Excel's does). Keep the default style already
+   * built above rather than overwriting it from nothing. */
+  if (ITextHost_TxGetCharFormat(editor->texthost, &host_cf) == S_OK && host_cf)
   {
     ZeroMemory(&cf, sizeof(cf));
     cf.cbSize = sizeof(cf);
-    cfany_to_cf2w(&cf, (CHARFORMAT2W *)host_cf);
-    ME_SetDefaultCharFormat(editor, &cf);
+    if (cfany_to_cf2w(&cf, (CHARFORMAT2W *)host_cf))
+      ME_SetDefaultCharFormat(editor, &cf);
   }
 
   eol_len = editor->bEmulateVersion10 ? 2 : 1;
